# Spacing Law

**Principle:** All spacing values (padding, margin, gap) must use multiples of 8px. Align with the 8pt grid (Material Design, Apple HIG).

## 8pt Grid — Baseline

**Preferred scale:** 8, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 96px. Optional half-steps (4px) for fine micro-adjustments only.

| Use Case | Value | rem |
|----------|-------|-----|
| Tight spacing | 8px | 0.5rem |
| Base unit | 16px | 1rem |
| Section padding (mobile) | 16px | 1rem |
| Standard padding | 24px | 1.5rem |
| Pill/container horizontal min | 32px | 2rem |
| Section padding (desktop) | 24–32px | 1.5–2rem |
| Large gaps | 40–48px | 2.5–3rem |

**Avoid:** 12px, 20px, 28px — these break the 8pt grid. Use 16px or 24px instead of 20px; 24px or 32px instead of 28px.

## Container & Page Padding

| Viewport | Min horizontal padding |
|----------|------------------------|
| Desktop (≥1024px) | 24px |
| Tablet (768–1023px) | 16px |
| Mobile (480–767px) | 16px |
| Small (320–479px) | 16px |

**Fluid alternative:** `padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.5rem)`

**Never:** Zero horizontal padding; content touching viewport edges.

## Anti-Patterns

- Spacing values not on 8pt grid (12, 20, 28px)
- Zero horizontal padding on containers

## Project Reference

This project: `STYLE-GUIDE.md` §1 (container vars), §18 (breakpoints). Container padding: 24px → 16px (768px) → 12px (480px). Section padding: 120px/80px/60px at breakpoints.
